TA-netqual
====

Collects per-interface link quality from /sys/class/net and /proc/net/dev: carrier/operstate, negotiated speed, MTU, cumulative RX/TX error and drop counters per physical interface (virtual/veth/lo excluded). Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype netqual:status) and netqual.<iface>_* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype netqual:metrics) at 60s cadence, with dashboards.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * none - pure /sys + /proc reads (no ethtool dependency)
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="netqual:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="netqual:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="netqual.*" by host
  | mstats avg("netqual.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=netqual:status  (per-iface JSON: speed_mbps, mtu, carrier, errors, drops)
Metrics: netqual.<iface>_<counter> on index=metrics (cumulative counters - use rate() in searches)
Alarm status when a physical interface reports no carrier.
Dashboards: TA-Netqual > Netqual Overview / Netqual Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-netqual/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * Speed is 0 in JSON/sysfs when the link is down.
  * Virtual interfaces (lo, veth*, docker*, br*, cni*) are excluded by name.

